From 152b18430b7313a5ea8b8bfe8054b32b3eae9e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:23:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Ctrl+Shift+1 to 4 take screenshots and recordings, and
 nothing else does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Luma's screenshot shortcuts, and the only ones:

- Ctrl+Shift+1 opens the screenshot tool as it was last used
  (show-screenshot-ui).
- Ctrl+Shift+2 captures the focused window (screenshot-window).
- Ctrl+Shift+3 opens the screenshot tool straight in Selection mode, ready to
  drag an area. GNOME has no action for that, so this adds
  show-screenshot-ui-area and ScreenshotUI.openArea(). It differs from
  Ctrl+Shift+1 whenever the tool was last left on Screen or Window.
- Ctrl+Shift+4 opens screen recording (show-screen-recording-ui), and stops a
  recording in progress.

GNOME's Print, Shift+Print, Alt+Print and Ctrl+Shift+Alt+R defaults are
removed. The whole-screen capture (screenshot) has no shortcut and is no
longer listed in Settings › Keyboard › Screenshots, which lists the four
above, in key order, named "Open the screenshot tool", "Capture a window",
"Drag to capture an area" and "Record the screen". The defaults live in the Shell's 00_org.gnome.shell.gschema.override
and in the new key's schema default.

For people whose own settings still hold GNOME's old defaults, or the values
set by hand on staging machines before this shipped, a user oneshot resets
those keys to the image defaults once. It is
luma-screenshot-shortcuts-migrate.service in graphical-session.target, with a
marker in ~/.local/state/luma/migrations. Any other value is a person's own
choice and is kept.

No shortcut Luma ships uses Ctrl+Shift+1 to 4: the Shell and Mutter, Tiling
Shell, Filer (Nautilus), Ptyxis and the Luma apps were checked.

Dropping this patch restores GNOME's shortcuts; the migration never runs
without it.
